1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,030
This is my uncle's story. In the Derg
years, he was a sailor in the navy.

2
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:09,860
The work was heavy. Sleep was four
hours, at most.

3
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:14,910
But on Thursday, the ship would sail to
Massawa. To him, Massawa was like

4
00:00:14,910 --> 00:00:17,620
heaven.

5
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:24,290
On Tuesday, working deep in the belly of
the ship, his foot slipped.

6
00:00:25,290 --> 00:00:28,710
His ankle twisted. His arm broke.

7
00:00:30,290 --> 00:00:34,620
His commander, who loved him like a son,
told him: "You stay here. Rest."

8
00:00:37,290 --> 00:00:41,510
His heart broke. He lost all hope; it
felt like the end of the world.

9
00:00:43,290 --> 00:00:46,000
On Thursday morning, the ship left
without him.

10
00:00:49,290 --> 00:00:53,600
It never came back. His comrades, and
his commander, stayed with the sea.

11
00:00:56,290 --> 00:01:00,080
The fall that broke him that day was the
hand that saved his life.

12
00:01:03,290 --> 00:01:05,420
Today he preaches the gospel. He tells
everyone one thing: "Let God lead your

13
00:01:05,420 --> 00:01:07,860
life."
